%N A400378 Maximum number of consecutive integers in [n, 2*n] all satisfying omega(k) > log(log(k)), where omega(k) is the number of distinct prime divisors of k.
%H A400378 Thomas F. Bloom, <a href="https://www.erdosproblems.com/452">Erdős Problem 452</a>, Erdős Problems.
%o A400378 (PARI) a(n) = my(r=0, m=0); for(k=n, 2*n, r=if(omega(k)>log(log(k)), r+1, 0); m=max(m, r)); m;
%Y A400378 Cf. A001221, A074739.
%K A400378 nonn,new
%O A400378 2,1
%A A400378 _Seiichi Manyama_, Oct 29 2026
